{"openapi":"3.0.0","info":{"title":"PaxDb API","version":"6.1","description":"APIs for accessing PaxDb protein abundance data, the url prefix /v6 corresponds to version 6 of the PaxDb.","contact":{"name":"PaxDb Team","email":"paxdb.team@gmail.com"},"license":{"name":"MIT license","url":"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"},"x-logo":{"url":"/assets/paxdb_logo_no_ver.png","href":"https://pax-db.org","altText":"PaxDB Logo"}},"servers":[{"url":"/v6","description":"API"}],"tags":[{"name":"Find hemoglobin abundance across datasets","description":"\n### Steps\n\n1. **Find protein ID**\n   → [GET /disambiguate?q=hemoglobin](#tag/NameSearch/operation/searchProteins) → find the STRING  protein ID → **9606.ENSP00000199708**.\n\n2. **Retrieve abundances**\n   → [GET /abundances?ids=9606.ENSP00000199708](#tag/Abundances/operation/getAbundancesByProteinIds) -> get the abundances across all datasets.\n"},{"name":"Find homologs of an A.thaliana protein rbcL in other plants","description":"\n### Steps\n\n1. **Find taxonomic level**\n   → [GET /orthology/taxonLevels/3702.O03042](#tag/Orthology/operation/getTaxonLevels) → find the available taxonomy levels for Arabidopsis thaliana and chose Streptophyta (**35493**).\n\n2. **Retrieve COGs**\n   → [GET /orthology/cog/3702.O03042/35493](#tag/Orthology/operation/getCOGs) → to get the cluster of ortholog groups (COGs) at Streptophyta level and find NOG005010.\n\n3. **Retrieve homologs**\n   → [GET /orthology/homologs/NOG005010](#tag/Orthology/operation/getHomologs) → to get the homologous proteins in the same COG cluster at Streptophyta level, which includes rbcL homologs in other plants."},{"name":"Find abundances of the NOG005010 orthologs in leaf datasets","description":"\n→ [GET /abundances/ortholog/NOG005010?organ=LEAF&score=1](#tag/Abundances/operation/getAbundancesByOrtholog) to get the abundances of the cross-species orthologs in leaf datasets with score >= 1."},{"name":"Abundances","description":"Retrieve protein abundance data from various datasets and experiments."},{"name":"NameSearch","description":"Search for proteins by name to disambiguate and find matching entries."},{"name":"Orthology","description":"Query orthologous proteins across different species and taxonomy levels."},{"name":"Metadata : Protein Info/Mapping","description":"Retrieve protein information / map from UniProt Accession."},{"name":"Metadata : Dataset Info","description":"Get information about datasets available in PaxDB."},{"name":"Metadata : General LookUp","description":"Look up reference data like organs, species, and taxonomy levels."}],"x-tagGroups":[{"name":"⭐ Start Here","tags":["Find hemoglobin abundance across datasets","Find homologs of an A.thaliana protein rbcL in other plants","Find abundances of the NOG005010 orthologs in leaf datasets","Try it yourself 🚀"]},{"name":"References","tags":["NameSearch","Abundances","Orthology","Metadata : Protein Info/Mapping","Metadata : Dataset Info","Metadata : General LookUp"]}],"components":{"securitySchemes":{"apiKey":{"type":"apiKey","in":"header","name":"x-api-key","description":"API key for authenticating requests and rate limiting. Obtain your API key from the \"Request API Key\" button on the top right of this page."}},"schemas":{"ProteinSummary":{"type":"object","properties":{"species_id":{"type":"integer","example":3702},"string_id":{"type":"string","example":"3702.O03042"},"preferred_name":{"type":"string","example":"rbcL"},"annotation":{"type":"string","example":"Ribulose bisphosphate carboxylase large chain; RuBisCO catalyzes two reactions: the carboxylation of D- ribulose 1,5-bisphosphate, the primary event in carbon dioxide fixation, as well as the oxidative fragmentation of the pentose substrate in the photorespiration process. Both reactions occur simultaneously and in competition at the same active site. Belongs to the RuBisCO large chain family. Type I subfamily."}},"required":["species_id","string_id","preferred_name","annotation"]},"DatasetDetail"